---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Cookies & Data Policy"
  description="How Naturo Group uses cookies, browser storage and similar technologies on this website."
  updated="27 April 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains how {site.legalName} ("we", "our", "us") uses cookies, browser
    storage and similar tracking technologies on the {site.name} website. It should be read
    alongside our <a href="/privacy-policies">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What is a cookie?</h2>
  <p>
    A cookie is a small text file that a website places on your device to store information.
    Similar technologies include local storage and session storage (browser-based key/value
    stores), pixels (tiny images used for tracking) and SDKs embedded by analytics or
    advertising providers.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Categories we use</h2>
  <h3>Strictly necessary</h3>
  <p>
    These are required for the site to function. We use browser <code>sessionStorage</code>
    to remember the contact details you have entered in our quote calculator so you do not
    have to type them twice. This data lives only in your browser tab and is cleared when
    you close it.
  </p>

  <h3>Analytics</h3>
  <p>
    We may use Google Analytics 4 to understand which pages are visited, how long visitors
    stay, and where traffic comes from. Analytics cookies are only set if you accept them
    in our cookie banner.
  </p>

  <h3>Marketing & retargeting</h3>
  <p>
    With your consent, we may use the Meta (Facebook/Instagram) Pixel and Google Ads tags
    to show you relevant advertising on those platforms. These tags create custom audiences
    based on actions taken on our site (for example, requesting a quote) so we can market
    our services to people who are interested in them.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Managing your preferences</h2>
  <p>
    You can decline non-essential cookies in our cookie banner the first time you visit and
    change your preference at any time. You can also:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Block or delete cookies in your browser settings.</li>
    <li>Opt out of personalised advertising via <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.com.au/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">youronlinechoices.com.au</a>.</li>
    <li>Opt out of Google Analytics with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.</li>
    <li>Adjust your Meta ad preferences inside Facebook / Instagram.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Disabling cookies may affect how the site functions; for example the quote calculator
    may not remember your details between page visits.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Lead capture data</h2>
  <p>
    When you submit your name, phone and email to view your instant price, that information
    is sent to our form intake provider (currently Formspree, formspree.io) and to any
    analytics or advertising tools you have consented to. The data is used to send your
    quote, follow up with you and, where you have consented, to market our services.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Updates</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as we add or remove tools. Material changes will be reflected
    in the "Last updated" date and surfaced through our cookie banner.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about cookies or data:<br />
    {site.legalName}<br />
    {site.abn}<br />
    Email: <a href={site.emailHref}>{site.email}</a>
  </p>
</LegalPage>
